       }
      ],
      "text": "ACS:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " for STEMI when primary PCI = ⍉STAT available (if ⍉contraindicated); fibrinolytics worsen outcome in unstable angina and NSTEMI."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "STEMI:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " tenecteplase = a single bolus over 5 seconds, reteplase a double bolus 30 minutes apart, alteplase an infusion over 90 minutes; tenecteplase and reteplase are used most often b/c they're simpler to give. Tenecteplase = dosed by wt, max 50 mg."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Interactions:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " other drugs that impair hemostasis raise the bleed risk; in ACS, GP IIb/IIIa inhibitors are ⍉recommended for pts receiving fibrinolytics."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "⍉IM injections and monitor for bleed; cholest embolization has been reported, so investigate any new embolic event."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
